@page "/"

<div class="hero">
    <div class="crumb" style="color:#cde8e4">Two-week MVP · .NET 8</div>
    <h1>Care records, appointments and clinic staff — in one vault.</h1>
    <p>Patients register, book and view records. Staff manage the floor. Administrators see the numbers. Built to the HealthVault SRS v1.1.</p>
    <a class="btn btn-light me-2" href="/login">Sign in</a>
    <a class="btn btn-outline-light" href="/register">Create a patient account</a>
</div>

<div class="stats">
    <div class="stat"><span>Auth</span><strong>JWT + roles</strong></div>
    <div class="stat"><span>Patients</span><strong>CRUD + search</strong></div>
    <div class="stat"><span>Appointments</span><strong>Status + slots</strong></div>
    <div class="stat"><span>Records</span><strong>Upload / view</strong></div>
</div>

<div class="card">
    <h3>Demo accounts (after first API start)</h3>
    <table class="table">
        <thead><tr><th>Role</th><th>Email</th><th>Password</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
            <tr><td>Administrator</td><td>admin@healthvault.com</td><td>Admin@12345</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Staff</td><td>staff@healthvault.com</td><td>Staff@12345</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Staff (nurse)</td><td>nurse@healthvault.com</td><td>Staff@12345</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Patient</td><td>patient@healthvault.com</td><td>Patient@12345</td></tr>
        </tbody>
    </table>
    <p class="mb-0 text-muted">Point the API at your SQL Server, run the scripts in <code>database/</code>, then start HealthVault.Api and HealthVault.Web.</p>
</div>
